[38;2;124;124;124mFind all functions f: R+ → R+ such that[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(f(w)² + f(x)²) / (f(y)² + f(z)²) = (w² + x²) / (y² + z²)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfor all positive reals w,x,y,z with wx = yz.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this. Let me set g(t) = f(t)² / t² or consider substitutions.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mLet me try setting w=x, y=z with wx=yz means w²=y² so w=y. Then trivially [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msatisfied.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me try the substitution. Let wx = yz = P (some product). [0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me try w=y, x=z: then wx=yz automatically. The equation becomes [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(f(w)²+f(x)²)/(f(w)²+f(x)²) = (w²+x²)/(w²+x²) = 1. Trivial.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me parametrize. Given product P, consider pairs (w,x) with wx=P. Write w = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m√P · a, x = √P/a for a>0. Then w²+x² = P(a² + 1/a²).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe equation says: for two pairs (w,x) and (y,z) with the same product P:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(f(w)²+f(x)²)/(f(y)²+f(z)²) = (w²+x²)/(y²+z²)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis means (f(w)²+f(x)²)/(w²+x²) is constant for all pairs (w,x) with wx=P. Call[0m[38;2;124;124;124mthis constant c(P).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo f(w)² + f(x)² = c(P)(w²+x²) whenever wx=P.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow let's use this. Fix product P. For w with x=P/w:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mf(w)² + f(P/w)² = c(P)(w² + P²/w²).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet h(t) = f(t)². Then h(w) + h(P/w) = c(P)(w² + P²/w²).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me substitute w = √P · s, so P/w = √P/s. Then:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mh(√P·s) + h(√P/s) = c(P)·P·(s² + 1/s²).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mHmm, let me define H(t) = h(t)/t² = f(t)²/t². Actually let me try a different [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mapproach.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me guess f(t) = kt for some constant k>0. Check: f(w)²+f(x)² = k²(w²+x²), [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mf(y)²+f(z)²=k²(y²+z²). Ratio = (w²+x²)/(y²+z²). Works! So f(t)=kt works.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAre there other solutions? Let me check if f(t)² must be proportional to t².[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFrom h(w)+h(P/w) = c(P)(w²+P²/w²).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me set P=1: h(w)+h(1/w) = c(1)(w²+1/w²).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me try to show h(t) = At² for some constant A.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTake two different products. Let's use the relation with general P.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mh(w) + h(P/w) = c(P)(w² + P²/w²). ...(*)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSet w = √P: 2h(√P) = c(P)·2P, so h(√P) = c(P)·P. Thus c(P) = h(√P)/P.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSubstitute back: h(w) + h(P/w) = (h(√P)/P)(w² + P²/w²).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet u = w, v = P/w, so uv = P, √P = √(uv). [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mh(u) + h(v) = (h(√(uv))/(uv))(u² + v²).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo h(u)+h(v) = h(√(uv))·(u²+v²)/(uv) for all u,v>0.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me set v=1: h(u)+h(1) = h(√u)·(u²+1)/u = h(√u)·(u+1/u).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mHmm. Let me try u=v: 2h(u) = h(u)·2u²/u² = 2h(u). Trivial.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me set u = t², v = 1: h(t²) + h(1) = h(t)·(t²+1)/t²·... wait let me [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mrecompute. (u²+v²)/(uv) with u=t²,v=1: (t⁴+1)/t². So h(t²)+h(1) = h(t)·(t⁴+1)/[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mt².[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mHmm, this is getting complicated. Let me try assuming h(t) = At² + B for some [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mconstants. Check the relation h(u)+h(v) = h(√(uv))(u²+v²)/(uv).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLHS = A(u²+v²) + 2B.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mRHS = (A·uv + B)(u²+v²)/(uv) = A(u²+v²) + B(u²+v²)/(uv).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor LHS=RHS: 2B = B(u²+v²)/(uv) for all u,v. If B≠0, then (u²+v²)/(uv) = 2 for [0m
