[38;2;124;124;124mform At²+B, only B=0 works. But I need to show h must be of this form, or more [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mgenerally that h(t)/t² is constant.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me define φ(t) = h(t)/t² = (f(t)/t)². Then h(t) = t²φ(t).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe relation: u²φ(u) + v²φ(v) = uv·φ(√(uv))·(u²+v²)/(uv) = φ(√(uv))(u²+v²).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo u²φ(u) + v²φ(v) = (u²+v²)φ(√(uv)).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis must hold for all u,v>0. [0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSet u=v: 2u²φ(u) = 2u²φ(u). Trivial.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSet v=1: u²φ(u) + φ(1) = (u²+1)φ(√u).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me set u = s²: s⁴φ(s²) + φ(1) = (s⁴+1)φ(s). ...(**)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mHmm. Let me try to show φ is constant.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFrom u²φ(u)+v²φ(v) = (u²+v²)φ(√(uv)).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis says φ(√(uv)) is a weighted average of φ(u) and φ(v) with weights u² and [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mv²:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mφ(√(uv)) = (u²φ(u)+v²φ(v))/(u²+v²).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me set a = ln u, b = ln v, and define ψ(s) = φ(e^s). Then √(uv) = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124me^{(a+b)/2}, so:[0m
